        "redock_ligand_resname": "TOP",
        "ph": 7.4,
        "notes": "E. coli K-12 DHFR (folA) with trimethoprim and NADPH at 1.90 A, single chain A. Added because the 7MYM/2W3A pair was not the controlled comparison it was presented as: 7MYM is 3.04 A with NAP (oxidised) while 2W3A is 1.50 A with NDP (reduced), so the pair differed in resolution and in cofactor oxidation state at once. Against 2W3A this entry matches the cofactor exactly and cuts the resolution gap from 1.54 A to 0.40 A. 7MYM is deliberately retained so the baseline offset can be measured against it rather than assumed away: in the first run every bacterial target sat near -6.3 while 2W3A alone sat at -7.69, flat across ligand size, which is the signature of a receptor artefact rather than selectivity. The entry also holds GOL and CL, both deliberately dropped. Residues 160-165 are an expression tag. Manna et al., Nat Commun 12:2949 (2021), doi:10.1038/s41467-021-23191-z.\n"
      },
